      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should show the committer timestamp which is the time when this exact commit was created. This can differ from the author timestamp if a commit was rewritten e.g. by amending or rebasing it.\n\nThe author timestamp is the time when the first version of a change was committed, it stays unchanged when the commit is rewritten e.g. by amending or rebasing it, the committer timestamp is always updated when the commit is rewritten.\n\nWe may consider to also show the last modified timestamp of the working tree version (currently shown in the compare view as \"local\" without commitid and timestamp).",
      "revId": "09d403b07732f4214fd8c791ba8d6d1515e407a2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
